A||N||11||Eric_PA||Heads on 3.4 block||||1||
Z||000000||Eric_PA||02-01-2001||06:51 AM||||I have been doing the searches on this swap and can't find any straight forward advice about the stock Camaro heads. Can they be used instaed of the Fiero heads or do you have to transplant them too with the Fiero intake?<BR>Eric||||reg||1
Z||000001||Alex4mula||02-01-2001||08:56 AM||||They are exactly the same as Fiero Heads (pushrod 3.4).||||reg||1
Z||000002||tgowens||02-01-2001||10:36 AM||||leave the heads on the 3.4L block, just move everything from the heads up over from the 2.8L........(saves having to replace head gaskets!)||||reg||1
Z||000003||Black88GT||02-01-2001||11:33 AM||||But you might as well replace the head gaskets while your doing the engine, it would be a PITA if you had to do it while the engine is in the car, plus you already have the 3.4 disassembled...<P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/cartmanico.gif">             <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/kennyico.gif">           <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/stanico.gif">         <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/kyleico.gif">             <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/chefico.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Will||02-01-2001||02:49 PM||||How do the heads on the Minivan 3.4's compare to the Camaro/Fiero heads for power/flow?||||reg||1
Z||000005||Formula88||02-01-2001||03:42 PM||||Has anyone checked into a 3400 SFI transplant?  It's the GenIII now used in the Grand Am, etc.  Rated at 175HP in the GA GT and 185 in the Montana.  Might be a better starting point than the F-body 3.4.  I've got a 99 Grand AM with the 3400 and it's a sweet engine, very flat torque curve and revs easily to it's 6000rpm redline.  <P>------------------<BR>When you choke a smurf, what color does it turn?||||reg||3
Z||000006||Eric_PA||02-02-2001||07:00 AM||||Thanks for all the info guys. It has been very halpful. I found a local salvage yard with three 1993+ 3.4's for $650 a piece. Is this a good deal? They told me they are all + or - 15K of 30K miles. Thats including everythin on the engine. It looks like I may get one and take the heads off have them pocket ported and a three angle valve job. All the goodies that can be done to the head keeping the spending moderate. I have to look arround for a good cam to use, but it looks like I will be working towards this.<BR>Thanks,<BR>Eric<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000007||ironhedno3||02-02-2001||08:13 PM||||the 3.4 from minivans and grand ams are different from the heads up..different piston also||||reg||1
Z||000008||Shaun41178||02-02-2001||10:10 PM||||How many times must it be said on this forum?  If a 2.8 or 3.1 or 3.4 came with aluminum heads it can not be a direct drop in for our iron head v6 engines.  An dagain you just can't swap the heads from our fieros on them as the compression will be too low.<P>if you use the whole computer and DIS system then yes you can plant a aluminum head engine in a Fiero but its still not a direct swap.  The dogbone mount will have to be moved or reworked.<P>Talk to countiblis for info on a aluminum head engine in a Fiero as he has it done||||reg||1
Z||000009||Will||02-02-2001||11:26 PM||||Don't take that tone with me, young man.<P>I asked how the aluminum heads are for power and flow. I am well aware of the compression/fitment issues.<BR>If I do a 3.4 swap, it will be with a minvan 3.4 precisely because of the DIS and roller cam. I am just wondering how the alluminum heads compare with the iron heads. Do they have D shaped exhaust ports? Round? Oval? Combustion chamber shape/octane tolerance? If they give better octane tolerance at the same compression, then it would be well worth it to use the aluminum heads instead of the iron heads on a Hi-Po application, wouldn't it?<BR>I don't care if the fiero intake transfers. I care about how much performance and/or economy the end result will have. That's another reason to use the DIS engine: the ECM has an economy cruise function for better gas mileage.||||reg||1
Z||000010||GT Bastard||02-03-2001||09:18 AM|||| <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000011||Shaun41178||02-03-2001||06:33 PM||||port shape of the heads depends on what model the engine is.  if a 3100 or a 3400 then it is a gen 3 and they have the D shaped exhaust ports.  intake ports look the same.  Flow from the Gen 3 heads flow more then the Gen 2 al heads.  The aluminum heads flow more then the iron heads too.  so the Gen 3 heads flow much more then Fiero heads.  thats stock for stock mind you.<P>i gave Travis a Gen 2 head to do some flow testing on to see how much cfm they actually flow.  Since NRT has flow tested a stock iron head and ported iron head Fiero head we will be able to see and compare stock for stock and to the modified heads.<P>Hope that answers your question Will.<P>------------------<BR>Shaun 85 GT with nitrous<BR>0-60 in 5.6 seconds<BR><A HREF="http://members.aol.com/Shaun41178" TARGET=_blank>Preferred Performance</A>||||reg||1
